xpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T12:27:04-07:00","id":1140276,"title":"","content":"Great stuff, I take it this is replacing your Mythology thread from earlier this year?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T12:38:10-07:00","id":1140281,"title":"","content":"That's very impressive. Like, I could see that in a book quality.<br /> <br /> Two thoughts come to mind. First, the relationship between God and the Exarchs. I hesitate to draw the comparison as the real world beliefs are more complex, but as a character in a mythology, God comes across as kinda Exarch-y. As an aside there's a quick reference in Seers of the Throne to the last Father cult before Paternoster being destroyed along with the Roman destruction of Jerusalem. I get that you're probably going for God being beyond the Supernal, but it's implied that before the Diadochi, the Awakened don't really understand the Exarchs and it fits quite well.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I've really wanted a lost era for Solomon, and this really fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T23:28:50-07:00","id":1140433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103498-my-cofd-blog?p=1140276#post1140276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great stuff, I take it this is replacing your Mythology thread from earlier this year?</div> </div> </div> </div>you mean the God Did It! thread? well, the purpose behind each of the projects is kinda different- the thread was meant to bring fourth ideas about setting an harsh truth based around Abrahamic religion. This project is not meant to claim to create an historic Era which still keeps things open for interpretation. Most of the material in the mythology thread could still be used, with and without the Era- so it is not as much as replacing things as it is about creating a parallel path, more or less.<br /> <br /> Anyway- glad you like it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T23:45:50-07:00","id":1140437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103498-my-cofd-blog?p=1140281#post1140281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very impressive. Like, I could see that in a book quality.<br /> <br /> Two thoughts come to mind. First, the relationship between God and the Exarchs. I hesitate to draw the comparison as the real world beliefs are more complex, but as a character in a mythology, God comes across as kinda Exarch-y. As an aside there's a quick reference in Seers of the Throne to the last Father cult before Paternoster being destroyed along with the Roman destruction of Jerusalem. I get that you're probably going for God being beyond the Supernal, but it's implied that before the Diadochi, the Awakened don't really understand the Exarchs and it fits quite well.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I've really wanted a lost era for Solomon, and this really fits.</div> </div> </div> </div>first, thanks for your kind words! I really do enjoy writing this Era, so I'm glad others enjoy reading it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second, yeah, I have thought about the &quot;Exarch like&quot; nature of God myself while writing this Era- but for obvious reasons I've decided to not go that way. After all, one of the things which really annoyed me during the Dark Eras Anthology was the story which established having some of the most important prophets of the bible as tools of the God Machine (it really &quot;grinds my gears&quot;, so to speak)- so I've decided to totally ignore this part. In order to avoid making God identified as one of the villainous Powers that Be, no matter if as an Exarch, God Machine, True Fae or whatever, I've decided to put Him outside of the regular sphere of powers, as its own thing. Notice that I've said &quot;outside&quot; instead of &quot;above&quot;- there is only one mention of powers higher than the Supernal in the text, and it is in the Prophets section- which <i>claim </i>to be powered by God. While they do serve Him, the source of their powers seems to be quit different. Even according to the bible the Israelite weren't the only ones with prophets, after all- so maybe those prophets who serve God are no different than the mages who devote themselves to Him. As for the Father Cult- we still have a lot of time before it needs to show up in the setting. We are still at the First Temple, while it was destroyed in the Second. I may put hints for the future foundation of it, but it would be many years before it would be established.<br /> <br /> In sort, I'm going to take the path of &quot;God is different&quot; in everything which is related to the project- not necessary &quot;above&quot; as much as on the &quot;outside&quot;. I do plan on adding a sidebar about it in the finished project- something in the likes of &quot;if you want, God could be the Father, or the God Machine, or the Principle or any other supernatural power which we already have in the setting- but I'm not going to make that choice for your own game. It's your choice to make&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T03:22:39-07:00","id":1140471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order to avoid making God identified as one of the villainous Powers that Be, no matter if as an Exarch, God Machine, True Fae or whatever, I've decided to put Him outside of the regular sphere of powers, as its own thing. </div> </div> </div>I think if you were careful you could actually get away with the God=Exarch, if you leaned into religions as lived traditions as opposed to fundamentalist statements about the world. Like, in the real world, the Exodus is pretty well regarded as being a myth (and one with some rather incoherent elements), however, it's still a powerful story that lots of people have used to articulate their own oppression. The literal identity of the being in the Bible is less important than what people do with those stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T04:09:27-07:00","id":1140482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103498-my-cofd-blog?p=1140471#post1140471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think if you were careful you could actually get away with the God=Exarch, if you leaned into religions as lived traditions as opposed to fundamentalist statements about the world. Like, in the real world, the Exodus is pretty well regarded as being a myth (and one with some rather incoherent elements), however, it's still a powerful story that lots of people have used to articulate their own oppression. The literal identity of the being in the Bible is less important than what people do with those stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying I can't do it- I'm saying I don't want to. I don't want to make a being that many people in the world believe in as a literal symbol of tyranny. What you are saying is true- the identity of the entity in question is less important than what people do with it, which is why I am planning on writing that sidebar about how to adapt God into your game, being used as Exarch included- but I am not going to establish God as being a force of selfish tyranny and human flaws as the canon of the Era, anymore than that I would make Hindu gods into demons or Norse deities into &quot;simply spirits&quot;. The gods are a mystery, and should be treated as such, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T07:11:39-07:00","id":1140509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want to make a being that many people in the world believe in as a literal symbol of tyranny. </div> </div> </div>Neither do I. My point is that your version of God is not unfair to the biblical character, but that's not exactly the God that most people believe in. Like, a lot of people think of the biblical stories as allegories to varying degrees and the ones who think of them literally true are probably not going to like you turning them into a game setting in the first place.<br /> <br /> Keeping God's identity mysterious isn't exactly helpful either, because they're still acting in the setting in a way that a lot of people are going to find odd. You've already fictionalised God as a rather weird inscrutable and kinda sinister entity with the Holy of Holies bending space and time and being filled with demons... It's a little late to stop is my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I am not going to establish God as being a force of selfish tyranny and human flaws as the canon of the Era, anymore than that I would make Hindu gods into demons or Norse deities into &quot;simply spirits&quot;. The gods are a mystery, and should be treated as such, IMO. </div> </div> </div>The Awakening eras don't shy away from doing that, and by not properly addressing the issue, your setting is a little light in comparison. Admittedly that's not necessarily a problem, but it does make the era feel more like Hunter stylistically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T07:30:06-07:00","id":1140512,"title":"","content":"The only thing I can say is that I have my own style of writing, and there are things I am willing and not willing to do. For now, the First Temple is not an exclusive Mage Era, so I can live with it not being the same style as other Mage settings. The concept of Solomon binding demons to his will and using them to build the Temple is not something that I've made up, so I again have little qualms about doing so- those things like the twisting of space or the whispers of bound demons are traits of Solomon, his builder, not of God himself (there are angels in the Temple too, after all- and nothing was said about the Holy of Holiest itself, only about the corridors of the Temple). God has to be adapted differently because the canon setting is not monotheistic, so I can play with things a little bit- but no, I'm not making God as an entity which is <i>objectively bad</i> as the Exarchs are. I'm not setting harsh truths because I don;'t like them, and I can't satisfy everyone who would read the Era. I can only do what that feel right in my eyes, and with all of the respect, I can't see a way in which I'll be reading such an Era myself and won't end up grinding my teeth. Again, I still remember my feeling when I've read that story from Tales of the Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> In sort, if you want to make God into an Exarch, I'm not going to stop you- I may even suggest you how to do it. But I'm not going to do it in my own setting or my own writing, especially since we don't need it. Rose has said more than once that in a Vampire setting, the chances are that God, the biblical character, probably exist, even if not in the way it is told in the book- and I believe the same would be valid for Hunter. We can have God and the Exarchs in the same setting and nothing bad would happen, IMO. As I said, it is not that I can't do it- I don't want to, like, at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:38:05-07:00","id":1140647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1103498-my-cofd-blog?p=1140512#post1140512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not setting harsh truths because I don;'t like them, and I can't satisfy everyone who would read the Era. I can only do what that feel right in my eyes, and with all of the respect, I can't see a way in which I'll be reading such an Era myself and won't end up grinding my teeth. Again, I still remember my feeling when I've read that story from Tales of the Dark Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, one last post and then I'll be quiet.<br /> <br /> By not setting any hard truths I think you've ended up halfway, you've translated a biblical era into mostly mage terms and then stopped. I understand wanting to respect real world beliefs, but you're not really doing that. You already crossed that line when God turned up in your setting.<br /> <br /> I'm not actually saying you need to make God an Exarch, that was meant more as an example (mostly 'cause it's a bit obvious), but I think the piece is weakened by not having the confidence to stake out a position on what God is or how they fit with mage cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T15:02:25-07:00","id":1140654,"title":"","content":"Ok, so you think that the way I represent God does not respect real world beliefs, and that by avoiding giving God a definite existence in Mage's terms I weaken my setting. I don't really agree with the first part, but I don't really care much about it right now- after all, in the end, I can only write things I love and passionate about, and that include the way God exist in the setting. With the second part, about &quot;not having the confidence&quot; to giving God an exact nature harming the setting, I strongly disagree- because I have placed God inside Mage's cosmology. A Mystery. As I've said in the piece, God is THE Mystery of the setting. He is the most non understood thing in the whole Era, for both Israelite, Canaanite and foreigners. Investigating what God actually <i>is</i> is a big part of what a Mage is going to do in the Era- they are going to try to get to the Holy of Holies, they are going to anger Solomon and try to bypass the guard of priests, demons and angels. They are going to have to withstand the space twisting effects of the building and the powers of a great sorcerer king, fighting prophets and challenging holy men. And maybe, if the storyteller is kind enough, they would discover the answer. God is a Mystery- and just as the setting Mysteries are usually left open for the Story teller to decide them, that is the path I've chosem. Not out of lack of confidence, but because I think that making up who and what God is should be the ST's job, and that it should be the player's role to find out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:02:16-07:00","id":1142153,"title":"","content":"I'm happy to present to you my next blog post, and the last post about vampires- <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/chapter-12-on-the-other-side-of-the-grave-the-living/\" target=\"_blank\">the Living</a>! I'm not sure, however, that I'll manage to make a new one next week, but I'll do my best. Anyway, the next post would be about Promethean in the First Temple, so you what to look for. In the next few hours, I would also finish my sum up post, which is sort of a compendium to everything which I've worked on in this blog until now. Hope you'll find it useful!<br /> <br /> Edit- I'm happy to add the new version of the sum up post, the <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/manuscript-2-vtr-core-book/\" target=\"_blank\">manuscript</a>. Check it out if you need something to organize the different blog posts. It also includes my full To Do List- so check it out and say what would you like to see!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-21-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T15:03:46-07:00","id":1142314,"title":"","content":"Awesome! thank you LostLight! <br /> Quick question: what is TF:V?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T18:27:44-07:00","id":1142369,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Task_Force:_VALKYRIE\" target=\"_blank\">Task Force: Valkyrie</a>, a Hunter Conspiracy that operates under the US Military, sort of. They've got high-tech military gear for Endowments, much of it experimental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T18:44:01-07:00","id":1142372,"title":"","content":"Thanks nofather!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T02:18:32-07:00","id":1142843,"title":"","content":"<br /> So here is a narrowed down version of my To Do list from the Manuscript section, divided into 3 tiers by how strong is the concept I have for each. Please tell me if there is something you would especially like to see!<br /> <br /> <u><i>Tier 1</i></u><ul><li>Daywalker- what that happens once that a vampire gains an immunity to their banes</li> <li>Persephone's Shadow- setting material about the First Regret</li> <li>Mumvuri Update- working on a modern version of the Clan</li> <li>Ahranite Brotherhood- a version of VII without VII</li> <li>Shadows of Smoke- variant Strix breeds</li> <li>Blood Dolls- rework as a micro template</li> <li>More Hunters- making another Hunter org from my To Do lists (see signature)</li> <li>Fire Fighters- Enen no Shouboutai adaption</li> <li>Carnival of Freaks- working on a new template from my to do list (see signature)</li> </ul><i><u>Tier 2</u></i><ul><li>Occult Matrix Sorcery- tools for mortals to mess with the God Machine's gears</li> <li>Fall of the Black Nathaniel- fiction</li> <li>the Gray- developing one of the lesser realms from the GMC together with a new Daemon lesser template</li> <li>the Other Place- developing the realm of mirrors using my Eidolon template</li> <li>Lost Visage- Mechanics for the vampiric effect</li> <li>Fog of Ages- presenting the old idea with a new light, including new antagonists</li> <li>Coven of Nanja- update to 2E to be used in the First Temple Dark Era</li> <li>Naditu- update to 2E to be used in the First Temple</li> <li>Mastema- mysterious power which devours the souls of the dead</li> <li>Alu- souls of a Lost Clan which cling to the dead and give them double edged gifts</li> <li>Lodge of Foul Dogs- Ghost Wolves Lodge for the First Temple</li> <li>Scorpion Host- shards of a primordial divinity of poison and purity</li> <li>Children of the Cacophony- Malakavia like condition which tunes to the changes in the Cacophony</li> <li>Clavicularius- 2E Legacy Update</li> <li>Prophets- variant Mage splat, using the Chronicler's Guide</li> <li>Void Spirit- the strange entities which dance among the stars</li> <li>Starspawn- mummy like creatures birthed by strange stars and inhuman kingdoms</li> <li>First Among the Fae- a Neolithic version of Changeling</li> <li>Project Freelancer- RvB adaption</li> </ul><i><u>Tier 3</u></i><ul><li>Anti Infrastructure- a way for mortals and demons to make their own free Hell</li> <li>Dark Realm of the Crossroads- developing a realm and a template based around a lesser known realm from the GMC</li> <li>Strix Hunter- developing the strix hunter version of VII</li> <li>Bureau of Silence- full writeup to the Covenant</li> <li>Bureau of Childer- new writeup to the Covenant</li> <li>Revolutionary Council- full Covenant writeup</li> <li>Lillian Heresy- full Covenant writeup</li> <li>Metronome- full writeup as an Angel</li> <li>Line of Solomon- new Proximi Dynasty</li> <li>Line of Saul- new Lucid Dynasty</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T05:07:49-07:00","id":1146624,"title":"","content":"and I'm happy to present to you this week's blog post-<a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/2017/10/04/open-development-5-it-is-not-good-for-the-man-to-be-alone-ptc/\" target=\"_blank\"> Promethean in the First Temple!</a> I've did some very controversial thought experiments when I wrote down this Era, from including some of my homebrew material to having some changes to the Created society in the setting, so tell me what do you think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T09:26:16-07:00","id":1147071,"title":"","content":"so I've just finished my weekly homebrew from my &quot;To Do&quot; list, and I'm happy to present you the Starspawn, a.k.a, my own version to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1147068-the-visitors-variant-expanded-template\">Visitors</a>. Check it out, and say what you think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T00:51:45-07:00","id":1149022,"title":"","content":"I'm happy to present to you the first <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/2017/10/12/chapter-13-mercurial-flesh-werewolves-part-1/\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf </a>post. I think I've got some interesting insight about a possible physical model for the Uratha- it just nice to see how well I can apply scientific models to a gameline and still get something which, more or less, makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:56:55-07:00","id":1151005,"title":"","content":"and here is the new Open Development post- <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/2017/10/19/open-development-6-you-shall-not-take-the-name-of-the-lord-your-god-in-vain/\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling in the First Temple</a>! Feel free to share your opinion about the post!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/bro